1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:06,005
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:13,596
[Camia] <i>Friends, she's finally</i>
<i>back in Ardiente.</i>

3
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,016
<i>My daughter, Lily Cruz!</i>

4
00:00:16,099 --> 00:00:17,058
[gasps and laughter]

5
00:00:17,142 --> 00:00:18,768
[Loring] <i>Is that you, Lily?</i>

6
00:00:19,602 --> 00:00:23,815
[Emilia] <i>I want you to witness</i>
<i>Lily Cruz being buried alive.</i>

7
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:27,360
<i>It's just one phone call away.</i>

8
00:00:29,446 --> 00:00:30,905
[Ivy] <i>Maybe we should postpone</i>

9
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:33,408
<i>the assassination</i>
<i>of Lily Cruz and Madrigal.</i>

10
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:36,619
<i>We have to make Arnaldo look good.</i>

11
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:37,787
<i>That's what he needs right now.</i>

12
00:00:37,871 --> 00:00:39,497
<i>Emilia, stop the operation.</i>

13
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:42,125
<i>Dad, I already told our men</i>
<i>to proceed with--</i>

14
00:00:42,208 --> 00:00:43,334
<i>Stop it now!</i>

15
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:44,586
[Ivy] <i>This is a peace agreement.</i>

16
00:00:44,669 --> 00:00:49,215
<i>From this day on, the killing, cheating,</i>

17
00:00:49,299 --> 00:00:51,760
<i>and blackmailing between Diego Torillo</i>

18
00:00:51,843 --> 00:00:54,054
<i>and Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo will stop.</i>

19
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:57,015
[Arnaldo] <i>For a peaceful election!</i>

20
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:58,767
[cheering and applause]

21
00:00:58,850 --> 00:01:01,644
[Diego] <i>Your days of torturing Lily</i>
<i>and her family are over.</i>

22
00:01:01,728 --> 00:01:05,940
<i>Do you really think we're done</i>
<i>giving you a hard time?</i>

23
00:01:06,024 --> 00:01:07,692
<i>You're the only one who still believes</i>

24
00:01:07,776 --> 00:01:09,152
<i>we should be scared of you, Emilia.</i>

25
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:12,822
<i>The moment justice prevails,</i>
<i>you'll get what you deserve.</i>

26
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:15,533
[Ivy] <i>That peace agreement</i>
<i>is the only thing</i>

27
00:01:15,617 --> 00:01:17,452
<i>stopping her from killing you.</i>

28
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:22,040
<i>Anna, you need that gun.</i>
<i>You have to protect yourself.</i>

29
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,124
[Jepoy] <i>What about you, Ivy?</i>

30
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,752
<i>After everything that happened,</i>
<i>are you still marrying Arnaldo?</i>

31
00:01:25,835 --> 00:01:30,131
[Ivy] <i>The wedding will proceed.</i>
<i>It needs to push through.</i>

32
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:34,552
Ivy, you don't have to do that.

33
00:01:34,636 --> 00:01:37,806
I'm here. We're all here.
We can bring the Ardientes down!

34
00:01:37,889 --> 00:01:40,183
You don't have to use yourself
as bait to catch Arnaldo!

35
00:01:40,266 --> 00:01:41,810
-Jepoy--
-What?!

36
00:01:42,852 --> 00:01:46,064
Diego, aren't you going to do something?

37
00:01:46,981 --> 00:01:50,777
Will you just stand there while
Ivy and Arnaldo get married?

38
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,320
-Jepoy.
-Hmm?

39
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:54,489
[Ivy] Jepoy, of all people,
shouldn't you be the one

40
00:01:54,572 --> 00:01:57,992
who understands
why I need to marry Arnaldo?

41
00:01:58,993 --> 00:02:01,037
I don't have to explain this to you again!

42
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:03,873
The wedding will push through.

43
00:02:03,957 --> 00:02:06,876
Whether you like it or not,
it's going to happen!

44
00:02:10,004 --> 00:02:11,172
I know.

45
00:02:11,256 --> 00:02:16,344
[unsettling music playing]

46
00:02:16,970 --> 00:02:18,555
There's nothing I can do anyway.

47
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:22,183
I just need to follow your plan.

48
00:02:23,143 --> 00:02:24,602
And you should.

49
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:31,776
[unsettling music playing]

50
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:39,659
Anna, go talk to him.

51
00:03:02,265 --> 00:03:04,976
You hate that Ivy will marry Arnaldo

52
00:03:05,476 --> 00:03:07,312
because until now, you still love her.

53
00:03:13,943 --> 00:03:16,571
You know why I did that, right, Anna?

54
00:03:18,781 --> 00:03:20,742
I know every member of that family.

55
00:03:20,825 --> 00:03:22,410
They're all demons.

56
00:03:22,994 --> 00:03:26,205
When they kidnapped me,
they caged and abused me.

57
00:03:26,706 --> 00:03:28,333
They treated me like an animal.

58
00:03:29,626 --> 00:03:32,128
They tortured me every single day.

59
00:03:33,296 --> 00:03:36,466
I can't let them do that to Ivy
if she gets caught.

60
00:03:37,508 --> 00:03:39,344
Ivy won't get caught.

61
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:46,434
Besides, you're in no position
to go against Ivy's plans.

62
00:03:46,517 --> 00:03:48,228
Why are you telling me this?

63
00:03:48,853 --> 00:03:50,188
Is it because…

64
00:03:51,147 --> 00:03:52,649
I'm just her friend?

65
00:03:54,651 --> 00:03:57,320
Because I'm just her friend,
I'm not Diego?

66
00:03:58,613 --> 00:03:59,697
And that Diego,

67
00:03:59,781 --> 00:04:03,117
just because I gave way
to let him love Ivy

68
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:05,745
doesn't mean I'll let Ivy
put herself in danger.

69
00:04:05,828 --> 00:04:07,372
What are you going to do, then?

70
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:09,332
I'll support her plan.

71
00:04:11,542 --> 00:04:15,421
But I'll find another way
to bring down the Ardientes.

72
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:24,138
Jepoy and Anna might not understand

73
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:25,848
but once I set my plans in motion,

74
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:29,185
they'll realize why I have
to go through with the wedding.

75
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:35,149
Are you sure about what you're doing, Ivy?

76
00:04:36,859 --> 00:04:39,112
[stutters] Yes I am, Diego.

77
00:04:41,781 --> 00:04:45,702
I'm very sure, and I'll need your help.

78
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:48,329
[suspenseful music playing]

79
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:58,214
[unsettling music playing]

80
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:09,392
[footsteps approaching]

81
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:11,394
Papa!

82
00:05:11,477 --> 00:05:14,230
You should come and celebrate with us.

83
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:17,859
Arnaldo's plan was a success.
He's on a roll.

84
00:05:17,942 --> 00:05:19,527
Oh, come here.

85
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:23,614
Do you still remember this?

86
00:05:26,242 --> 00:05:28,995
Yes, Papa. That's the map of our town.

87
00:05:29,078 --> 00:05:30,121
Yeah.

88
00:05:31,748 --> 00:05:35,793
Remember when we would
campaign at the plaza?

89
00:05:38,713 --> 00:05:40,506
[Julio] <i>The crowd would go crazy.</i>

90
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,718
<i>Everyone was happy and smiling.</i>

91
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:49,724
<i>They couldn't wait</i>
<i>to hang garlands on my neck.</i>

92
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:51,726
<i>And the others…</i>

93
00:05:52,435 --> 00:05:58,900
<i>they would wipe off my sweat</i>
<i>as if I was a saint.</i>

94
00:06:05,239 --> 00:06:06,449
[Julio chuckling]

95
00:06:07,116 --> 00:06:08,868
I remember that, Papa.

96
00:06:09,952 --> 00:06:13,206
We provided for our people.

97
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:16,125
We conditioned their minds…

98
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:19,587
bought what they needed…

99
00:06:20,546 --> 00:06:22,423
and we gave it to them.

100
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:28,221
We kept our people happy and contented.

101
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:31,474
But now…

102
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:42,318
those same people are the ones
attacking us from all sides…

103
00:06:43,277 --> 00:06:47,990
left and right, back and forth,
upside down.

104
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:52,161
We are getting hit from all sides.

105
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:56,290
How did this happen, Emilia?

106
00:06:59,877 --> 00:07:01,212
I know I--

107
00:07:02,797 --> 00:07:04,674
I know I've done…

108
00:07:06,676 --> 00:07:07,927
bad things.

109
00:07:08,803 --> 00:07:12,181
But I only did it to our enemies.

110
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:14,684
But now…

111
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:16,853
Diego…

112
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:20,690
Lily, Camia…

113
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:22,733
Madrigal.

114
00:07:25,486 --> 00:07:29,198
They won't stop until they destroy us.

115
00:07:30,825 --> 00:07:32,076
But Papa…

116
00:07:32,785 --> 00:07:34,745
we could have stopped this…

117
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:38,541
if only you didn't listen to Ivy Aguas.

118
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:40,668
[sighs]

119
00:07:41,961 --> 00:07:43,713
One day, Emilia…

120
00:07:45,673 --> 00:07:48,134
one day, we'll stop them all…

121
00:07:49,886 --> 00:07:52,555
but not in the way you're thinking.

122
00:07:53,764 --> 00:07:55,057
But for now…

123
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:59,479
I would like you to take care
of one of our enemies.

124
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,527
Kill Jaguar.

125
00:08:06,819 --> 00:08:08,821
[suspenseful music playing]

126
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:11,532
For the sake of our family.

127
00:08:11,866 --> 00:08:14,452
[ominous music playing]

128
00:08:14,535 --> 00:08:15,661
[sighs]

129
00:08:23,461 --> 00:08:25,838
I'm not really used to fighting.

130
00:08:27,632 --> 00:08:29,300
But when I saw Emilia,

131
00:08:30,092 --> 00:08:33,721
I remembered all the terrible
things she did to you and Ivy.

132
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:37,642
I felt like I was the one
she hurt firsthand.

133
00:08:40,686 --> 00:08:43,814
Emilia shouldn't have
talked to you like that.

134
00:08:44,690 --> 00:08:47,693
I'm sorry that you got dragged into this.

135
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:49,445
No, it's fine.

136
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:56,244
By the way, thank you
for defending me from Emilia.

137
00:08:59,205 --> 00:09:01,582
Anna, I should be the one thanking you.

138
00:09:02,124 --> 00:09:07,755
You risked your life to protect
my daughter's real identity.

139
00:09:07,838 --> 00:09:12,093
You don't know how big
of a sacrifice you're making

140
00:09:13,010 --> 00:09:16,806
just so Lily can continue
her fight against the Ardientes.

141
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,646
I'm also doing this for Nanny Carlotta.

142
00:09:25,523 --> 00:09:29,652
Anna, you can count on my support.

143
00:09:31,362 --> 00:09:34,407
And I won't allow anyone to hurt you.

144
00:09:35,241 --> 00:09:37,785
I'll protect you like my own daughter.

145
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:44,625
[melancholic music playing]

146
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:52,633
[unsettling music playing]

147
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:55,803
JAGUAR TAKES OVER
THE ARDIENTES' TURF

148
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:06,314
MASKED GAMBLING LORD
FACING THE ARDIENTES HEAD-ON

149
00:10:09,650 --> 00:10:11,193
[Jepoy] <i>Who are you, Jaguar?</i>

150
00:10:12,278 --> 00:10:14,739
<i>I need you in my fight</i>
<i>against the Ardientes.</i>

151
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:18,242
[tense music playing]

152
00:10:28,419 --> 00:10:30,796
So, you're really going to kill Jaguar?

153
00:10:31,172 --> 00:10:32,340
Can you do it?

154
00:10:34,342 --> 00:10:35,426
[sighs]

155
00:10:37,178 --> 00:10:38,846
That's what Papa ordered me to do.

156
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:43,309
Your father has given you a lot of orders

157
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:45,227
but you've ignored most of them.

158
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:46,979
Something is different now.

159
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:48,689
For the first time,

160
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:51,025
he talked to me without mocking me.

161
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,362
I also noticed a lot of changes in you

162
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:56,739
ever since you started
dealing with Jaguar.

163
00:10:57,448 --> 00:10:58,616
You look more beautiful.

164
00:10:59,575 --> 00:11:00,785
And you're sexier too.

165
00:11:02,703 --> 00:11:03,746
Raul, please.

166
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:13,756
Are you really doing all this for Jaguar?

167
00:11:14,131 --> 00:11:16,133
[slow tense music playing]

168
00:11:17,009 --> 00:11:18,386
Once I run out of patience…

169
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:22,807
I'll have him killed myself.

170
00:11:22,890 --> 00:11:27,395
[unsettling music playing]

171
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,022
Go to bed, Raul. I have to make a call.

172
00:12:04,515 --> 00:12:08,185
Arnaldo, do you remember
how back in the day,

173
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:10,604
even when you were kids,

174
00:12:10,688 --> 00:12:13,149
you and Diego always used to fight a lot?

175
00:12:13,899 --> 00:12:15,901
And you'd always end up winning

176
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,195
no matter what the fight was about.

177
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:23,159
And that is really what you did
at the last press conference.

178
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:26,912
You gave him a good beating. That's good!

179
00:12:26,996 --> 00:12:28,289
Thank you, Grandpa.

180
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:29,874
You know, now I'm thinking…

181
00:12:30,791 --> 00:12:33,502
we should push through with the debate

182
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:38,132
so you can completely demolish that loser.

183
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:40,342
Okay. I'm game.

184
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:44,221
[Julio] This really calls
for a celebration.

185
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:45,222
Imagine…

186
00:12:45,764 --> 00:12:49,101
Arnaldo is ahead of Diego.

187
00:12:49,894 --> 00:12:53,522
And, of course, my dear daughter, Emilia,

188
00:12:53,606 --> 00:12:57,067
is about to terminate Jaguar.

189
00:12:59,945 --> 00:13:03,699
I've never been so proud of this family.

190
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:07,411
-Long live, Ardiente.
-Long live, Ardiente.

191
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:12,208
[ominous music playing]

192
00:13:21,842 --> 00:13:22,885
[Arnaldo] Thank you.

193
00:13:26,305 --> 00:13:28,682
[Marlon] <i>Those Ardientes are at it again.</i>

194
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:30,851
They canceled the first debate.

195
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:33,062
But now, they want to schedule a new one?

196
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:35,147
[Anna] Are we going to do it?

197
00:13:35,231 --> 00:13:38,359
Diego, are you ready to face
the Ardientes again?

198
00:13:40,194 --> 00:13:41,612
I've always been ready.

199
00:13:42,488 --> 00:13:47,201
I'm not hiding anything.
They won't find any dirt on me.

200
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:49,203
And this is actually a good thing,

201
00:13:49,286 --> 00:13:51,997
so I can finally present
my platform to the public.

202
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:58,379
But, Diego, they canceled the first debate

203
00:13:58,462 --> 00:14:00,631
because they were afraid
of being implicated

204
00:14:00,714 --> 00:14:02,091
in the murder of Nimfa.

205
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:04,843
It won't happen again.

206
00:14:04,927 --> 00:14:09,014
Once I find an opening,
even the smallest opportunity,

207
00:14:09,098 --> 00:14:12,393
I will reveal
the Ardientes' darkest secrets.

208
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:19,525
[tense music playing]

209
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:37,668
[unsettling music playing]

210
00:14:48,762 --> 00:14:51,140
You can't say no to me, Jaguar.

211
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:53,642
[phone chimes]

212
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:58,772
Perfect.

213
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:08,240
-[screams]
-[gunshot]

214
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:11,827
<i>Let go of me!</i>

215
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,792
[Emilia] <i>Jaguar saved my life.</i>

216
00:15:18,876 --> 00:15:21,295
<i>So, why would he kill me right away?</i>

217
00:15:21,378 --> 00:15:22,504
<i>A cellphone?</i>

218
00:15:23,088 --> 00:15:24,924
<i>"Call me, my beautiful".</i>

219
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:27,092
<i>Jaguar's quite the sweet-talker, isn't he?</i>

220
00:15:28,969 --> 00:15:32,389
[Raul] <i>You should know</i>
<i>how obsessed I am with you.</i>

221
00:15:33,974 --> 00:15:38,479
<i>That's why I saved you</i>
<i>from Natalie, remember?</i>

222
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:40,397
[Emilia] <i>Obsessed?</i>

223
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:43,359
[Raul] <i>I want to steal you away</i>
<i>from your husband.</i>

224
00:15:45,361 --> 00:15:49,907
[unsettling music playing]

225
00:15:52,493 --> 00:15:54,954
Well, it was nice while it lasted.

226
00:15:55,871 --> 00:15:58,415
But some good things really never last.

227
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:01,168
Well, not in Poblacion Ardiente.

228
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:14,264
[unsettling music swells]

229
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:17,476
Ping!

230
00:16:17,977 --> 00:16:19,061
Jaguar.

231
00:16:30,781 --> 00:16:32,324
And I'm ready to go.

232
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:43,502
[ominous music playing]

233
00:17:01,770 --> 00:17:02,813
Jaguar.

234
00:17:07,568 --> 00:17:08,902
Emilia.

235
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:36,513
[ominous music playing]

236
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:54,656
Jaguar…

237
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:57,284
Who are you?

238
00:17:58,577 --> 00:18:05,584
[ominous music intensifies]

239
00:18:13,342 --> 00:18:14,510
Don't touch that.

240
00:18:15,219 --> 00:18:16,970
You don't know what's in there.

241
00:18:17,054 --> 00:18:18,764
It might bite you.

242
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:29,024
[suspenseful music playing]

243
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:31,527
[Emilia grunts]

244
00:18:42,162 --> 00:18:43,789
Who are you?!

245
00:18:49,628 --> 00:18:51,296
[grunts]

246
00:18:54,049 --> 00:18:55,092
Jaguar.

247
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,223
[tense music playing]

248
00:19:08,313 --> 00:19:09,481
[car engine starts]

249
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:16,238
Jaguar!

250
00:19:16,572 --> 00:19:17,739
[car engine revving]

251
00:19:18,740 --> 00:19:19,992
Jaguar!

252
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:23,203
[tense music playing]

253
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:29,710
[car door closes]

254
00:19:37,801 --> 00:19:38,844
There you go.

255
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:42,306
Hon, this tie looks good on you!

256
00:19:42,389 --> 00:19:44,266
Why don't you wear it tomorrow?

257
00:19:44,349 --> 00:19:46,435
I have a feeling
it'll be your lucky charm.

258
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:48,645
Why?

259
00:19:50,647 --> 00:19:51,732
Well…

260
00:19:52,065 --> 00:19:54,568
I guess you don't need a lucky charm.

261
00:19:55,110 --> 00:20:00,490
I'm sure you'll wipe the floor
with Diego after the debate.

262
00:20:02,951 --> 00:20:04,661
Is that what you really think?

263
00:20:05,370 --> 00:20:06,622
-[Ivy chuckles]
-Huh?

264
00:20:07,581 --> 00:20:08,665
Is it?

265
00:20:09,499 --> 00:20:10,584
Hon!

266
00:20:10,959 --> 00:20:14,588
Yes, it's what I really think.
And that hurt.

267
00:20:22,721 --> 00:20:24,348
I'm sorry. I just wanted to be sure.

268
00:20:25,557 --> 00:20:26,600
Sorry.

269
00:20:27,309 --> 00:20:28,936
-Sorry.
-Hon.

270
00:20:29,311 --> 00:20:30,354
Sorry.

271
00:20:31,355 --> 00:20:32,606
I was just making sure.

272
00:20:33,815 --> 00:20:36,276
[tense music playing]

273
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:54,294
[tense music intensifies]

274
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:05,722
[alarm goes off]

275
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:06,807
<i>Emilia?</i>

276
00:21:07,224 --> 00:21:08,225
<i>Hmm?</i>

277
00:21:08,308 --> 00:21:09,810
[alarm continues beeping]

278
00:21:09,893 --> 00:21:12,062
[Raul] <i>I set my alarm wrong again.</i>

279
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:24,032
[Raul] <i>So, you're really going</i>
<i>to kill Jaguar?</i>

280
00:21:24,616 --> 00:21:25,575
<i>Can you do it?</i>

281
00:21:25,659 --> 00:21:27,327
<i>That's what Papa ordered me to do.</i>

282
00:21:27,411 --> 00:21:29,705
<i>Your father has given you a lot of orders</i>

283
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:31,665
<i>but you've ignored most of them.</i>

284
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:40,465
[phone ringing]

285
00:21:45,304 --> 00:21:47,431
[phone ringing]

286
00:21:53,395 --> 00:21:54,271
Hello?

287
00:21:55,731 --> 00:21:56,773
Raul?

288
00:21:57,482 --> 00:21:59,693
Where are you? I need to talk to you.

289
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,570
I'm here at home.

290
00:22:03,071 --> 00:22:05,073
<i>Emilia… my love…</i>

291
00:22:05,157 --> 00:22:06,616
What's going on?

292
00:22:07,075 --> 00:22:08,827
<i>Do you know what time it is? It's late.</i>

293
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:10,370
<i>You know, I need to rest.</i>

294
00:22:10,454 --> 00:22:13,832
I'm meeting some clients tomorrow morning.

295
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:16,543
<i>So if you don't need me</i>
<i>for anything important…</i>

296
00:22:16,835 --> 00:22:18,670
you should let me go to bed.

297
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:22,174
Okay, fine. Good night.

298
00:22:22,424 --> 00:22:23,633
Okay, good night.

299
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:30,640
[tense music playing]

300
00:23:09,596 --> 00:23:10,555
[car engine stops]

301
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:14,267
[car door closes]

302
00:23:15,018 --> 00:23:16,061
Jaguar!

303
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:40,627
[suspenseful music playing]

304
00:23:47,092 --> 00:23:48,802
Jenny, where's my husband?

305
00:23:48,885 --> 00:23:50,137
I don't know, ma'am.

306
00:23:50,220 --> 00:23:53,014
Jeez, you never know anything! Get lost!

307
00:23:57,686 --> 00:23:59,187
Let's see if you're here, then.

308
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:06,736
[suspenseful music intensifies]

309
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:10,824
[knocks on door]

310
00:24:10,907 --> 00:24:12,033
Raul?

311
00:24:12,784 --> 00:24:13,785
Raul.

312
00:24:16,454 --> 00:24:17,539
Hey.

313
00:24:19,583 --> 00:24:20,792
Where have you been?

314
00:24:28,466 --> 00:24:29,801
<i>Rufo…</i>

315
00:24:29,885 --> 00:24:31,052
<i>I need your help.</i>

316
00:24:37,893 --> 00:24:40,020
<i>Rufo, take me to the mansion now.</i>

317
00:24:41,146 --> 00:24:42,230
<i>Let's go.</i>

318
00:24:43,648 --> 00:24:44,649
[car door closes]

319
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:48,737
What are you talking about?

320
00:24:48,820 --> 00:24:49,821
I'm right here.

321
00:24:49,905 --> 00:24:51,573
I'm in our house, taking a bath.

322
00:24:51,656 --> 00:24:53,200
Did you just come in?

323
00:24:53,283 --> 00:24:54,409
What do you mean?

324
00:24:54,492 --> 00:24:56,203
We just spoke on the phone, remember?

325
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:58,622
I told you I was going to bed.

326
00:24:58,705 --> 00:25:01,166
I'm just taking a bath first.

327
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:06,129
Hold on. What's the problem?
Is something wrong?

328
00:25:07,255 --> 00:25:08,798
Nothing.

329
00:25:09,674 --> 00:25:11,551
Wait up, Emilia.

330
00:25:14,512 --> 00:25:16,932
Don't you want to join me in here?

331
00:25:21,186 --> 00:25:23,188
-No.
-Come on, Emilia.

332
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:25,565
Hop in.

333
00:25:26,608 --> 00:25:28,568
Come here.

334
00:25:28,652 --> 00:25:29,653
Emilia.

335
00:25:30,737 --> 00:25:31,863
Emilia.

336
00:25:36,826 --> 00:25:38,787
[tense music playing]

337
00:25:54,469 --> 00:25:56,930
[drums playing]

338
00:25:57,347 --> 00:25:59,641
[man] Diego for a new Ardiente!

339
00:25:59,724 --> 00:26:06,064
[chanting] Diego, Diego! Diego, Diego!

340
00:26:06,147 --> 00:26:07,315
I'm okay.

341
00:26:07,399 --> 00:26:09,776
Diego, my little brother. Are you ready?

342
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:15,740
I think I should be the one
asking you that.

343
00:26:16,241 --> 00:26:17,284
Are you ready, brother?

344
00:26:17,367 --> 00:26:18,159
[chuckles]

345
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:21,246
I just thought you might
back out like the first debate.

346
00:26:21,329 --> 00:26:24,708
Well, I must admit you're
giving me one hell of a fight.

347
00:26:25,166 --> 00:26:28,586
But I'm confident the people of
Ardiente will still vote for me.

348
00:26:32,465 --> 00:26:33,550
Let's see.

349
00:26:38,179 --> 00:26:39,597
[Amelia sighs loudly]

350
00:26:40,724 --> 00:26:41,808
Hon…

351
00:26:42,309 --> 00:26:44,436
I need to make a call
to the office in Manila.

352
00:26:44,519 --> 00:26:45,562
Okay, sure.

353
00:26:45,645 --> 00:26:46,688
-Excuse me.
-I'll stay here.

354
00:26:46,771 --> 00:26:47,772
Yeah.

355
00:26:49,357 --> 00:26:51,735
[tense music playing]

356
00:26:54,779 --> 00:26:56,698
[cell phone buzzing]

357
00:27:02,162 --> 00:27:03,121
[Diego, whispering] Ivy.

358
00:27:03,204 --> 00:27:04,289
Diego…

359
00:27:06,458 --> 00:27:07,834
Good luck later.

360
00:27:08,293 --> 00:27:10,170
I know you've got this.

361
00:27:11,254 --> 00:27:13,965
For the future of Poblacion Ardiente.

362
00:27:21,222 --> 00:27:24,809
[tense music continues playing]

363
00:27:37,364 --> 00:27:44,371
[people chanting]
Diego Torillo for real change!

364
00:27:55,673 --> 00:27:58,843
You can't help but
be jealous of me, can you?

365
00:27:58,927 --> 00:28:01,638
Ever since we were kids,
you've always wanted what I had.

366
00:28:03,348 --> 00:28:05,058
Mom's love…

367
00:28:05,141 --> 00:28:06,893
Grandpa's love…

368
00:28:07,727 --> 00:28:08,770
and Ivy.

369
00:28:09,396 --> 00:28:12,565
Now, you want to steal my position.

370
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:15,443
But don't worry.

371
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:20,073
I'll make you taste
the bitter sting of defeat.

372
00:28:21,032 --> 00:28:23,493
That way, you'll start thinking twice

373
00:28:23,576 --> 00:28:25,203
about pushing through with your campaign.

374
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:26,579
You know what, Mayor?

375
00:28:27,539 --> 00:28:30,125
Less talk, more action.

376
00:28:35,797 --> 00:28:36,840
Hon…

377
00:28:38,133 --> 00:28:44,180
[tense music playing]

378
00:28:45,056 --> 00:28:46,057
Come.

379
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:54,065
[Marlon] Batch, don't mind him.

380
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:56,818
He's acting that way because
he knows he's going to lose.

381
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:58,486
You've got this in the bag.

382
00:28:58,570 --> 00:29:02,031
Arnaldo's no different
from the rest of the Ardientes.

383
00:29:02,115 --> 00:29:03,700
They thrive in violence and bloodshed.

384
00:29:03,783 --> 00:29:05,660
They don't know how to fight fair.

385
00:29:06,870 --> 00:29:09,748
But today, I'll make sure…

386
00:29:10,915 --> 00:29:12,167
that he loses.

387
00:29:24,429 --> 00:29:28,224
[TV announcer] <i>Live from</i>
<i>Poblacion Ardiente Auditorium…</i>

388
00:29:28,308 --> 00:29:32,604
<i>The biggest face-off that</i>
<i>everyone has been talking about.</i>

389
00:29:32,687 --> 00:29:35,774
<i>The Poblacion Ardiente Public Debate!</i>

390
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:40,111
[emcee] Please welcome,
our debate facilitator,

391
00:29:40,195 --> 00:29:42,489
the one and only Ka Tunying,

392
00:29:42,572 --> 00:29:44,324
Anthony Taberna!

393
00:29:44,407 --> 00:29:50,997
[cheers and applause]

394
00:30:04,052 --> 00:30:06,054
<i>Good day, everyone.</i>

395
00:30:06,888 --> 00:30:09,724
Thank you for coming here today

396
00:30:10,099 --> 00:30:12,352
for the Poblacion Ardiente Public Debate.

397
00:30:12,435 --> 00:30:18,191
[cheers and applause]

398
00:30:21,277 --> 00:30:26,825
With us today are the contenders
for the gubernatorial post.

399
00:30:27,325 --> 00:30:30,912
Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo!

400
00:30:30,995 --> 00:30:37,710
[cheers and applause]

401
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:39,462
[audience chanting] Ardiente forever!

402
00:30:41,548 --> 00:30:43,716
Go get him, tiger.

403
00:30:43,925 --> 00:30:45,844
[chanting continues]

404
00:30:45,927 --> 00:30:47,262
Boo-yah!

405
00:30:47,637 --> 00:30:53,226
[chanting continues]

406
00:30:54,435 --> 00:30:55,645
Sir.

407
00:30:55,728 --> 00:30:56,938
-Good day.
-And to you.

408
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:03,528
And we also have his opponent…

409
00:31:03,611 --> 00:31:06,865
Mr. Diego Ardiente-Torillo!

410
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:12,328
[cheers and applause]

411
00:31:13,037 --> 00:31:17,542
[audience chanting]
<i>Diego Torillo for real change!</i>

412
00:31:18,793 --> 00:31:21,421
[chanting continues]

413
00:31:22,005 --> 00:31:22,964
Good luck!

414
00:31:23,673 --> 00:31:29,971
[chanting continues]

415
00:31:38,688 --> 00:31:43,234
We will discuss several issues,
including the problems

416
00:31:43,318 --> 00:31:45,361
<i>being faced by our province.</i>

417
00:31:45,904 --> 00:31:48,823
<i>Our contenders need to explain</i>

418
00:31:48,907 --> 00:31:50,700
how they will solve these problems

419
00:31:50,783 --> 00:31:53,745
should they be elected to office.

420
00:31:56,122 --> 00:31:58,166
Gentlemen, are you ready?

421
00:31:58,249 --> 00:31:59,417
Yes, sir. I'm ready.

422
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:02,170
But I don't know if my brother,
Diego Torillo, is.

423
00:32:02,253 --> 00:32:03,296
Are you?

424
00:32:04,047 --> 00:32:05,381
[Anthony] <i>Mr. Torillo?</i>

425
00:32:05,465 --> 00:32:06,549
Yes, I'm ready.

426
00:32:09,844 --> 00:32:10,970
[Anthony] All right then.

427
00:32:11,054 --> 00:32:12,221
Let's begin.

428
00:32:12,305 --> 00:32:18,061
[cheers and applause]

429
00:32:21,606 --> 00:32:24,192
We'll have an exciting debate today

430
00:32:24,275 --> 00:32:26,444
because we're going to find out

431
00:32:26,527 --> 00:32:29,238
what's in the minds and hearts
of our two candidates.

432
00:32:29,906 --> 00:32:31,699
But before we begin…

433
00:32:31,783 --> 00:32:33,451
<i>I'd like to remind our candidates</i>

434
00:32:33,534 --> 00:32:37,997
<i>that you have 90 seconds</i>
<i>to answer in each round.</i>

435
00:32:38,081 --> 00:32:43,211
Then, we'll give you
60 seconds each for rebuttal,

436
00:32:43,294 --> 00:32:47,632
and another 30 seconds to
counter the opponent's comments.

437
00:32:48,091 --> 00:32:50,176
<i>Lastly, you'll hear a sound to inform you</i>

438
00:32:50,259 --> 00:32:53,137
<i>that you only have</i>
<i>10 seconds left to answer.</i>

439
00:32:53,221 --> 00:32:54,847
Is everything clear, gentlemen?

440
00:32:54,931 --> 00:32:56,683
-Yes, it's clear.
-Loud and clear.

441
00:32:58,935 --> 00:33:02,563
Very good. Now, here's our first question.

442
00:33:03,314 --> 00:33:07,568
Let's talk about the economy.
Poblacion Ardiente is known

443
00:33:07,652 --> 00:33:10,822
<i>as the fruit and vegetable bowl</i>
<i>of the country.</i>

444
00:33:11,406 --> 00:33:14,617
What projects will you implement

445
00:33:14,701 --> 00:33:19,288
to further improve the
economic status of the province?

446
00:33:20,623 --> 00:33:22,291
I'll go first, Mr. Anthony.

447
00:33:23,167 --> 00:33:26,004
<i>Throughout the whole duration</i>
<i>of my service as mayor,</i>

448
00:33:26,087 --> 00:33:31,175
I've implemented many projects
for my constituents,

449
00:33:31,259 --> 00:33:35,805
<i>which brought investors</i>
<i>from Manila and other countries.</i>

450
00:33:36,639 --> 00:33:39,851
First, I launched
the Export Processing Zone

451
00:33:39,934 --> 00:33:43,146
which was a big help
to Poblacion Ardiente's economy.

452
00:33:45,606 --> 00:33:46,691
"A big help"?

453
00:33:49,360 --> 00:33:50,903
<i>What help are you talking about?</i>

454
00:33:51,904 --> 00:33:54,574
I think you meant the project
was a big help to your family.

455
00:33:54,657 --> 00:33:58,369
There might be many projects
implemented in this town,

456
00:33:58,453 --> 00:34:01,039
but the people
didn't benefit from them at all.

457
00:34:01,581 --> 00:34:07,336
<i>So in my opinion, you can't say</i>
<i>that our town is progressive</i>

458
00:34:07,420 --> 00:34:09,672
when only a certain few
benefit from new projects.

459
00:34:12,508 --> 00:34:16,512
If I become the governor of this province,

460
00:34:17,096 --> 00:34:20,266
<i>I promise to help each</i>
<i>and every one of you.</i>

461
00:34:20,933 --> 00:34:23,686
I will help every resident
of Poblacion Ardiente

462
00:34:23,770 --> 00:34:25,855
set up their own businesses.

463
00:34:26,564 --> 00:34:30,818
<i>That way, not only our town will improve,</i>

464
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:32,779
<i>but your lives as well.</i>

465
00:34:33,488 --> 00:34:36,657
I believe that the people are the key

466
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:38,409
to having a progressive province.

467
00:34:39,202 --> 00:34:41,162
So, we should prioritize their welfare.

468
00:34:41,454 --> 00:34:42,497
[scoffs]

469
00:34:42,580 --> 00:34:44,540
-[Diego] <i>Thank you very much.</i>
-[cheers and applause]

470
00:34:45,458 --> 00:34:50,046
[audience chanting]
Diego Torillo for real change!

471
00:34:53,049 --> 00:34:54,884
[chanting continues]

472
00:34:54,967 --> 00:34:58,638
[cheers and applause]

473
00:35:00,223 --> 00:35:02,975
[Anthony] <i>You all heard</i>
<i>Diego Torillo's answer.</i>

474
00:35:03,684 --> 00:35:06,521
After discussing the economy,
let's ask them about

475
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:09,148
their respective platforms for education.

476
00:35:12,318 --> 00:35:13,653
Mr. Anthony, before I answer that,

477
00:35:13,736 --> 00:35:17,532
let me just give a comment
on Diego's answer.

478
00:35:19,075 --> 00:35:20,660
<i>I don't know why he couldn't remember,</i>

479
00:35:20,743 --> 00:35:23,579
<i>but the whole time the Ardientes</i>
<i>have served this town,</i>

480
00:35:23,663 --> 00:35:26,666
we've been implementing
projects for the poor.

481
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:28,501
Okay?

482
00:35:28,584 --> 00:35:29,335
<i>But…</i>

483
00:35:29,418 --> 00:35:31,754
I'm not sure why you don't get it, Diego.

484
00:35:32,505 --> 00:35:34,632
Well, I guess it's because
of your lack of expertise

485
00:35:34,715 --> 00:35:39,011
since you haven't held
any government positions before.

486
00:35:40,263 --> 00:35:43,432
Before we can implement
projects for the people,

487
00:35:43,516 --> 00:35:50,356
we first need to have political
and business connections.

488
00:35:50,439 --> 00:35:51,607
But wouldn't it be better

489
00:35:51,691 --> 00:35:53,734
if our lives would all improve together?

490
00:35:54,527 --> 00:35:56,988
<i>The old, the young, the rich, the poor,</i>

491
00:35:57,071 --> 00:35:58,406
<i>businessmen or farmers.</i>

492
00:35:59,574 --> 00:36:00,950
How can we do that?

493
00:36:01,033 --> 00:36:04,871
Through a system
of all-inclusive governance.

494
00:36:05,705 --> 00:36:10,960
We should help the poor,
give free tuition to students,

495
00:36:11,043 --> 00:36:14,672
and raise funds to build
more schools and hospitals.

496
00:36:15,173 --> 00:36:16,841
I believe that's possible.

497
00:36:17,842 --> 00:36:21,053
[ominous music playing]

498
00:36:54,754 --> 00:36:55,922
[Anthony] <i>Mayor Arnaldo?</i>

499
00:36:58,341 --> 00:37:04,388
[suspenseful music playing]

500
00:37:06,140 --> 00:37:09,227
Do you want to comment on
Mr. Torillo's answer?

501
00:37:13,814 --> 00:37:15,566
You're running out of time, Mayor.

502
00:37:15,650 --> 00:37:21,614
[timer beeping]

503
00:37:24,533 --> 00:37:25,910
[buzzer]

504
00:37:29,956 --> 00:37:31,082
Excuse me.

505
00:37:31,165 --> 00:37:32,208
Mayor?

506
00:37:32,792 --> 00:37:33,709
Mayor!

507
00:37:34,210 --> 00:37:35,127
[Anthony] What's happening?

508
00:37:35,211 --> 00:37:37,380
[indistinct murmuring]

509
00:37:37,463 --> 00:37:38,547
-Arnaldo?
-Mayor!

510
00:37:38,631 --> 00:37:39,882
[Emilia] Arnaldo!

511
00:37:39,966 --> 00:37:43,678
[indistinct chatter]

512
00:37:43,761 --> 00:37:45,304
[Emilia] Arnaldo!

513
00:37:45,388 --> 00:37:47,640
-[reporter 1] Mayor!
-[reporter 2] What happened, Mayor?

514
00:37:48,724 --> 00:37:50,559
-[woman] <i>Mayor!</i>
-[man] <i>Mayor!</i>

515
00:37:57,483 --> 00:37:59,819
Impressive, Mendoza.

516
00:37:59,902 --> 00:38:01,946
Impressive! Perfect!

517
00:38:03,197 --> 00:38:06,200
I'll transfer the money to your account

518
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:10,788
but make sure to share it
with the woman you hired.

519
00:38:11,747 --> 00:38:14,125
-Again, impressive!
-It's Ms. Aguas.

520
00:38:17,044 --> 00:38:19,213
[reporter] Ms. Aguas, may we
ask you a few questions?

521
00:38:19,297 --> 00:38:22,675
-It's okay. Yes?
-Could you give a statement

522
00:38:22,758 --> 00:38:24,677
regarding what happened
to Mayor Ardiente-Torillo?

523
00:38:25,094 --> 00:38:26,971
Why did he suddenly walk out?

524
00:38:30,141 --> 00:38:33,436
First of all, I'd like to apologize

525
00:38:33,519 --> 00:38:35,771
to Mayor Arnaldo's supporters

526
00:38:36,522 --> 00:38:40,484
because he didn't do well in his
debate with Diego Torillo.

527
00:38:43,362 --> 00:38:44,572
But I think…

528
00:38:45,865 --> 00:38:49,493
it's time the public learns…

529
00:38:50,119 --> 00:38:51,954
that my future husband…

530
00:38:53,622 --> 00:38:55,374
is going through something.

531
00:38:56,375 --> 00:38:58,627
What do you mean? Is the Mayor sick?

532
00:39:03,007 --> 00:39:05,843
I guess that's all I can say for now.

533
00:39:06,385 --> 00:39:07,595
Thank you.

534
00:39:07,678 --> 00:39:09,597
[reporter] <i>Ms. Aguas, a few</i>
<i>follow-up questions.</i>

535
00:39:09,680 --> 00:39:11,390
<i>Please, can you tell us more…?</i>

536
00:39:14,518 --> 00:39:17,313
What was that?! Huh?!

537
00:39:18,731 --> 00:39:19,815
You…

538
00:39:20,608 --> 00:39:22,610
were a disgrace.

539
00:39:24,528 --> 00:39:25,821
You…

540
00:39:25,905 --> 00:39:28,074
were a humiliation.

541
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:34,038
You didn't even lift a finger
to correct your mistakes!

542
00:39:34,121 --> 00:39:37,375
Thank goodness Ivy Aguas was there

543
00:39:37,458 --> 00:39:42,922
to cover for your inexcusable behavior!

544
00:39:44,048 --> 00:39:45,549
Julio, enough.

545
00:39:45,633 --> 00:39:46,884
No!

546
00:39:46,967 --> 00:39:48,386
He has to hear this.

547
00:39:49,428 --> 00:39:52,973
Do you know that because of what you did,

548
00:39:54,100 --> 00:39:57,061
it could cost you the election?

549
00:39:58,104 --> 00:40:02,358
Do you know what shame you have
brought to our family again?!

550
00:40:04,068 --> 00:40:05,152
No, no, no!

551
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:07,405
Allow me.

552
00:40:07,905 --> 00:40:11,158
I have to jolt him out of his dreams.

553
00:40:12,785 --> 00:40:14,036
[Julio laughing]

554
00:40:14,120 --> 00:40:15,579
You think you're so good?

555
00:40:15,996 --> 00:40:17,206
That debate…

556
00:40:18,249 --> 00:40:22,002
was supposed to be something
that was your forte!

557
00:40:22,878 --> 00:40:26,173
You were supposed to prove
that you were more intelligent,

558
00:40:26,257 --> 00:40:29,718
that you were stronger,
that you were better.

559
00:40:29,802 --> 00:40:31,137
You were supposed to prove

560
00:40:31,220 --> 00:40:36,016
that you were superior
over Diego in all aspects!

561
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,435
But no!

562
00:40:37,518 --> 00:40:38,644
What did you do?

563
00:40:38,727 --> 00:40:42,064
You turned yourself into a clown!

564
00:40:42,148 --> 00:40:44,150
You know how you looked like?

565
00:40:44,233 --> 00:40:47,653
You looked like an old coyote

566
00:40:47,736 --> 00:40:49,905
with your tail between your legs,

567
00:40:49,989 --> 00:40:52,825
a yellow streak written on your back,

568
00:40:52,908 --> 00:40:57,538
and your foot in your mouth
while everyone was laughing!

569
00:41:00,332 --> 00:41:01,333
[sighs]

570
00:41:02,418 --> 00:41:04,086
I don't understand why you're so mad.

571
00:41:04,170 --> 00:41:05,671
That was just a debate, okay?

572
00:41:05,754 --> 00:41:08,674
I have more opportunities
to win the people's vote!

573
00:41:08,757 --> 00:41:09,842
A press conference!

574
00:41:09,925 --> 00:41:12,678
With a press conference, they'll
forget about what happened.

575
00:41:12,761 --> 00:41:14,930
[scoffs] "With just a press
conference, they'll forget--"

576
00:41:16,932 --> 00:41:18,434
I trusted you!

577
00:41:18,809 --> 00:41:20,895
I trusted you so many times.

578
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:24,356
But every time, time and time again…

579
00:41:25,065 --> 00:41:27,568
you have always failed me!

580
00:41:29,862 --> 00:41:30,988
Leave!

581
00:41:31,363 --> 00:41:34,450
[tense music playing]

582
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:35,951
[Julio sighs]

583
00:41:43,709 --> 00:41:47,838
Your son's brain
is down there in his foot!

584
00:41:58,599 --> 00:42:00,768
[reporters] <i>Mayor! Mayor!</i>

585
00:42:01,644 --> 00:42:02,603
<i>Mayor!</i>

586
00:42:03,771 --> 00:42:05,022
<i>Mayor! Mayor!</i>

587
00:42:13,113 --> 00:42:14,198
[door opens]

588
00:42:18,369 --> 00:42:19,411
[door closes]

589
00:42:31,090 --> 00:42:32,132
Sit down.

590
00:42:34,301 --> 00:42:36,470
Grandpa, if you're just
going to scold me again, save--

591
00:42:36,554 --> 00:42:37,555
Please…

592
00:42:38,347 --> 00:42:41,350
sit down, Arnaldo.

593
00:42:42,268 --> 00:42:45,980
[unsettling music playing]

594
00:42:52,444 --> 00:42:53,487
You know…

595
00:42:56,031 --> 00:43:00,452
I have been thinking long and hard.

596
00:43:02,705 --> 00:43:07,793
I have been thinking
long and hard the whole night.

597
00:43:10,254 --> 00:43:11,422
And lately…

598
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:18,345
sleep has been eluding me.

599
00:43:21,640 --> 00:43:23,934
I would like to apologize.

600
00:43:26,478 --> 00:43:27,813
Now, don't get me wrong.

601
00:43:29,023 --> 00:43:33,402
My apology doesn't come without a price.

602
00:43:35,112 --> 00:43:37,156
Tell me the truth, Arnaldo.

603
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:42,703
What happened that you had
to walk out during the debate?

604
00:43:43,662 --> 00:43:44,747
Please tell me.

605
00:43:47,207 --> 00:43:48,500
I don't wanna talk about it.

606
00:43:49,001 --> 00:43:50,085
Arnaldo…

607
00:43:51,503 --> 00:43:53,380
I would like to help you.

608
00:43:54,256 --> 00:43:55,841
Tell me what happened.

609
00:43:57,426 --> 00:43:59,011
[shrill tone]

610
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:07,144
ARNALDO, CONFESS YOUR SINS.
YOUR CONSCIENCE WILL EAT YOU UP.

611
00:44:12,608 --> 00:44:13,400
[Ivy] <i>Why?</i>

612
00:44:14,234 --> 00:44:15,277
<i>-Hon.</i>
<i>-Hon?</i>

613
00:44:15,361 --> 00:44:17,112
<i>-Are you seeing this?</i>
<i>-What?</i>

614
00:44:17,196 --> 00:44:19,573
-<i>This. This. This!</i>
-[shrill tone]

615
00:44:24,828 --> 00:44:26,413
[shrill tone]

616
00:44:33,253 --> 00:44:37,007
[ominous music playing]

617
00:44:37,466 --> 00:44:39,885
[mumbling] She was there.
She was there. I was talking.

618
00:44:39,968 --> 00:44:41,762
And then, she was there.

619
00:44:41,845 --> 00:44:43,972
[mumbling incoherently]

620
00:44:44,056 --> 00:44:45,641
-She was there…
-Huh?

621
00:44:45,724 --> 00:44:47,518
I was there and then…

622
00:44:47,601 --> 00:44:49,061
-I don't even know…
-What?

623
00:44:49,603 --> 00:44:51,188
What's happening to you, Arnaldo?

624
00:44:51,271 --> 00:44:52,272
I don't…

625
00:44:54,358 --> 00:44:57,569
I don't, I don't know…

626
00:44:59,780 --> 00:45:01,740
[mumbling] I don't know
what's happening to me.

627
00:45:02,908 --> 00:45:04,493
[Arnaldo sobs] I don't even know…

628
00:45:04,576 --> 00:45:07,704
I don't even know if you're real!

629
00:45:08,831 --> 00:45:09,873
Huh?

630
00:45:10,290 --> 00:45:12,167
I don't even know if you're here!

631
00:45:13,460 --> 00:45:16,171
-What's wrong with you?
-I'm not, I'm not…

632
00:45:16,255 --> 00:45:18,382
What's happening? [sobbing]

633
00:45:18,966 --> 00:45:20,759
Carlotta, Nimfa…

634
00:45:22,594 --> 00:45:25,472
Carlotta, Nimfa…

635
00:45:26,723 --> 00:45:28,517
They're in front of me.

636
00:45:30,060 --> 00:45:31,895
They're in front of me.

637
00:45:33,522 --> 00:45:35,065
They're haunting me!

638
00:45:36,984 --> 00:45:38,360
They're haunting me.

639
00:45:39,820 --> 00:45:41,530
The people I killed…

640
00:45:44,283 --> 00:45:45,325
They're…

641
00:45:45,826 --> 00:45:47,286
They're right there.

642
00:45:49,455 --> 00:45:50,706
Their faces…

643
00:45:51,915 --> 00:45:53,000
They're alive!

644
00:45:55,002 --> 00:45:56,837
I don't know what's happening.

645
00:45:57,546 --> 00:45:58,922
I don't know what's real anymore!

646
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:00,924
I don't know if you're real!
I don't know if--

647
00:46:01,008 --> 00:46:02,509
I don't know if I'm here!

648
00:46:02,593 --> 00:46:05,929
I don't know! I don't know what to do!

649
00:46:06,472 --> 00:46:09,725
[sobs] I don't know what to do!
I'm losing it!

650
00:46:09,808 --> 00:46:11,685
-Arnaldo.
-I'm losing it!

651
00:46:11,768 --> 00:46:14,021
-Arnaldo.
-I'm losing it! Is this--

652
00:46:14,104 --> 00:46:15,272
Is this you?!

653
00:46:15,772 --> 00:46:17,483
-Arnaldo.
-I'm not sure anymore!

654
00:46:17,566 --> 00:46:20,360
-Arnaldo…
-I'm not sure! I don't know!

655
00:46:20,444 --> 00:46:22,738
[sobbing] I don't know!

656
00:46:22,821 --> 00:46:25,073
-Arnaldo.
-I don't know.

657
00:46:26,700 --> 00:46:28,202
I don't know.

658
00:46:28,285 --> 00:46:29,411
Arnaldo…

659
00:46:29,870 --> 00:46:31,121
Look at me.

660
00:46:32,748 --> 00:46:34,124
Arnaldo…

661
00:46:34,875 --> 00:46:37,461
Have you been taking your medicines?

662
00:46:37,544 --> 00:46:38,629
I don't--

663
00:46:40,672 --> 00:46:41,757
I…

664
00:46:42,549 --> 00:46:43,550
I killed them.

665
00:46:44,218 --> 00:46:46,053
Enough, enough, enough.

666
00:46:47,137 --> 00:46:49,389
Enough, my son. Enough.

667
00:46:49,473 --> 00:46:51,058
-I killed them.
-Enough.

668
00:46:51,141 --> 00:46:53,060
[sobbing] Grandpa, I'm sorry.

669
00:46:53,143 --> 00:46:55,229
-I'm sorry I failed you.
-No, no, no.

670
00:46:55,312 --> 00:46:57,189
-I failed you again.
-No, no.

671
00:46:57,272 --> 00:47:00,609
-I failed you.
-You did not, you did not.

672
00:47:00,692 --> 00:47:02,528
-[sobbing] I failed you.
-No, you did not.

673
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:05,989
I failed you so many times.
I don't know what's happening.

674
00:47:07,991 --> 00:47:09,785
I don't know what's happening.

675
00:47:10,410 --> 00:47:11,495
-I…
-It's okay.

676
00:47:11,578 --> 00:47:15,624
-[screaming]
-No, no, no. No!

677
00:47:15,707 --> 00:47:17,668
-[crying]
-No, Arnaldo. No, it's okay.

678
00:47:17,751 --> 00:47:19,294
It's okay, it's okay.

679
00:47:19,378 --> 00:47:22,005
-[sobbing]
-It's okay.

680
00:47:22,089 --> 00:47:24,091
-It's all right.
-[sobbing]

681
00:47:24,174 --> 00:47:26,468
-Go and rest.
-[sobbing]

682
00:47:26,552 --> 00:47:28,845
-Go and rest, okay? Go to sleep.
-[sobbing]

683
00:47:29,346 --> 00:47:31,473
<i>We'll talk again tomorrow, okay?</i>

684
00:47:32,140 --> 00:47:34,685
[Raul] <i>We need Madrigal in our group.</i>

685
00:47:34,768 --> 00:47:36,687
<i>Do you mean to tell me that Jaguar</i>

686
00:47:36,770 --> 00:47:39,273
<i>and that snot-nosed Diego are teaming up?!</i>

687
00:47:39,356 --> 00:47:40,691
<i>Bring me that man.</i>

688
00:47:40,774 --> 00:47:43,735
[Ivy] <i>If you could only see Arnaldo…</i>

689
00:47:43,819 --> 00:47:47,322
<i>All my plans are about to unfold.</i>

690
00:47:47,823 --> 00:47:49,616
[Arthur] <i>Twenty million pesos, Mayor.</i>

691
00:47:49,700 --> 00:47:53,161
<i>Or else, Ivy Aguas will die.</i>

692
00:47:54,204 --> 00:47:55,080
[Arnaldo] <i>Ivy!</i>

693
00:47:55,163 --> 00:47:57,499
<i>I will not be threatened by nobody.</i>

694
00:47:57,583 --> 00:47:58,750
[yells]

695
00:47:59,918 --> 00:48:01,086
<i>Where is Ivy?!</i>

696
00:48:01,169 --> 00:48:01,920
<i>I want to see Ivy!</i>

697
00:48:02,004 --> 00:48:02,754
<i>That she-devil?</i>

698
00:48:02,838 --> 00:48:05,090
<i>She's on her way to hell!</i>

699
00:48:05,173 --> 00:48:08,093
[theme music playing]
